  "worked_solution": "Notice that the function $p(x)$ is differentiable for all $x>-1.$ Therefore, the correct answer is $p(x)=\\sqrt{x+1}.$\n\nThe other functions are not differentiable at $x=1.$\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not defined at $x=1$ and hence it is not differentiable there.\n\n- The function $h(x)$ has a corner point at $x=1$ and hence it is not differentiable there.\n\n- The function $q(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x=1$ and hence it is not differentiable there.\n\n- The function $g(x)$ has a vertical tangent at $x=1$, and hence it is not differentiable there.",
